tonight the family of eric echevarrio  held a vigil to honor his life  after he was killed in a car crash on  wednesday eight news now reporter  madison kimbrough joins us live from the  memorial site near blue diamond in fort  apache  with more madison  yes tonight was about honoring eric's  life many  still not believing that he's actually  gone but the family  wants justice you know if you're going  to drink or  get high whatever you're going to do do  it in your house like don't drive he  took a  a dad from my 14 year old son he took my  husband my  my best friend my life partner my my  everything i don't even know what i'm  going to do without them  a visual was held tonight for 52 year  eric echeverria  who died last week after being hit by a  teen driver  that teen 19-year-old zeon collins is  being accused of driving under the  influence  and is facing several other charges my  family is hurting  they're in pain they feel that justice  hasn't been served  and i know it's too soon to speak but  we're hoping that  something does happen tonight friends  and family came out to honor eric's life  flowers balloons and pictures were all  set up along with music playing in the  background  family members and friends spoke briefly  before participating in a two-minute  moment of silence  you know it has taken a little bit for  it to sink in you know i'm still in  denial still in shock that  that he's gone so we're just setting  everything up making the arrangements  for  you know for our service echeveria was  described as a happy man  always smiling joking around with a  heart of gold  he was originally from new york but  spent the last 23 years here in las  vegas  he was an army vet and worked as a  custodian for the clark county school  district  for 18 years  and this is a look at his memorial site  right off of apache road  as for collins he was released with  electronic monitoring and is due in  court for a status check  on thursday january 7. reporting live  m